WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.191
Public repositories can provide legitimate technical context through source code,

00:00:04.191 --> 00:00:08.283
commit history, issue discussions, documentation, configuration examples, and release records.

00:00:08.283 --> 00:00:12.374
Package registries and container references can reveal public dependencies, versions,

00:00:12.374 --> 00:00:14.011
publishers, and distribution relationships.

00:00:14.011 --> 00:00:17.693
Documentation may identify domains, endpoints, product names, deployment patterns,

00:00:17.693 --> 00:00:18.921
or third-party services.

00:00:18.921 --> 00:00:23.421
Example configurations can clarify architecture, but they may be outdated, generic,

00:00:23.421 --> 00:00:25.876
or unrelated to a live environment.

00:00:25.876 --> 00:00:27.922
Preserve provenance and publication dates.

00:00:27.922 --> 00:00:34.059
Dependency clues help defenders understand software supply-chain exposure and identify components that need internal verification.

00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:37.332
A package name alone does not prove deployment.

00:00:37.332 --> 00:00:38.969
Forks, mirrors, abandoned projects,

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:42.242
and similarly named packages require careful identity checks.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:47.561
Accidental public exposure of a secret, token, or credential must be handled responsibly.

00:00:47.561 --> 00:00:50.015
Do not test or use it.

00:00:50.015 --> 00:00:54.107
Preserve only the minimum evidence needed under policy, restrict access,

00:00:54.107 --> 00:00:59.426
notify the authorized owner or approved reporting channel, and support revocation and cleanup.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.881
Repositories and registries have access rules.

00:01:01.881 --> 00:01:05.972
Public technical analysis does not authorize entry into private projects,

00:01:05.972 --> 00:01:09.654
use of leaked credentials, or retrieval of restricted artifacts.

00:01:09.654 --> 00:01:15.382
Stop at access boundaries and seek guidance when ownership or reporting authority is unclear.

00:01:15.382 --> 00:01:19.883
Report code and package findings as evidence with confidence and limitations.

00:01:19.883 --> 00:01:24.793
Connect them to internal inventories through authorized teams before asserting operational use,

00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:26.020
ownership, or vulnerability.
